      "value": "@{65f4b1a3d0a7a0c657a7d3a8|full_name} the issue was caused when I had 2 wrist_R bones in the same imported FBX, one was on the main armature and one was on a 2nd armature that was included along side with it, when using a parent constraint, it favored the wrist_R bone of the secondary armature rather than the primary armature, so the secondary armature wrist_R was binding to itself alone with the cube that was also binding to the secondary armature, and thus didn't move when in runtime despite the constraint being active, the problem was solved for me when I went back later and renamed all secondary bones to be distinguished from those on the primary armature (that being the armature with the humanoid rig)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
