      "value": "@{624740095e4d345280f70522|full_name}: Thanks for the extra info. Since I can't see the setup of your avatar, I'll still need a bit more info to reproduce this issue.\n\nI've attempted to follow your steps by creating an avatar with two identical armatures on it and then creating a parent constraint in Unity with its source set to the wrist bone on the first armature. It follows the movement of the first armature, which is the expected behavior.\n\nAre you comfortable with providing a full list of the steps you're following to trigger this problem, or alternatively recording a short video clip of what you're doing in Unity that causes it? Did you create the parent constraint yourself, or is it imported with the model or otherwise automatically created in some other way? If you made it yourself, how are you assigning its source transform?\n\nIf you click once on the Source Transform for your constraint, Unity will highlight the transform assigned as the source in the hierarchy view. Is it assigned to the correct armature?",
