  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "VRC Constraints cant distinguish between two transforms with the same name, I have two armatures with identically named bones, even after manually dragging and dropping all the correct transforms from the humanoid rig to the secondary rig, the secondary rig fails to properly bind itself, as it seems they are just using their own transforms due to being named identically, this is further backed up by adding a cube to my avatar that I bound to my right wrist, again making sure it was the proper humanoid rig VRC is using as the basis of my avi, and despite being the correct transform it still acted as if it was bound to the wrist of the secondary armature, it seems the VRC Constraints cant distinguish between transforms with identical names across an avi, and you have to just hope it chooses the right one, which for me it didn't",
